{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Are you jealous for me, etc.</b> Joshua, because he was young in years, seized hold of the trait of jealousy, as it is written: ״וַיַּעַן יְהוֹשֻׁעַ בִּן נוּן מְשָׁרֵת מֹשֶׁה מִבְּחֻרָיו״ — from the fact that he was among his young men, he said thus. And had he been old and advanced in years, he would not have been particular about two companions asserting themselves at once. And concerning this the Sages said (Bava Batra 75a): the countenance of Moses was like the countenance of the sun, and Joshua like the moon. For just as the moon lodged complaint and said: it is impossible for two kings to use a single crown, so too Joshua lodged complaint and said: Eldad and Medad are prophesying. But Moses was like the sun, which lodged no complaint at all; so too Moses said: Would that all the people of HaShem were prophets." "And he said, <b>for if HaShem would give His spirit upon them.</b> It is explained in the Akeidah: it is obvious that if they were to be apportioned from the spirit that is upon me, I would not be jealous of them — for every person is jealous except of his son and his disciple (Sanhedrin 105a). Rather, even ״if HaShem would give His spirit upon them״ and they would not be my disciples, in any case I would not be jealous of them. And there are those who say that he said precisely this — for precisely at the time that HaShem gives His spirit upon them can it be that all the people of HaShem would be prophets; but if He were to apportion upon them from the spirit that is upon me, it is impossible for them all to be prophets, for the one apportioned must resemble his apportioner from every side. And our Sages of blessed memory said (Nedarim 38a): the Shekhinah rests only upon one who is mighty, wise, rich, and humble — and all of these were in Moses. They desired in this: since all of them were in Moses, therefore the one apportioned from him must resemble him from every side. And this would be impossible — that all Israel be equal in all four of these attributes, for if so, what would distinguish one great man from another? But if HaShem gives His spirit upon them without an intermediary, then there is no need for these four attributes that they all be equal in them. And one cannot say that they would resemble Him as it were, for what likeness would you compare to Him? Therefore it says: ״כִּי יִתֵּן ה׳ אֶת רוּחוֹ עֲלֵיהֶם״."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:40:50.075456291Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}